    <section class="project">
      <h2>UTICA Radio Map</h2>
      <p>A web app that maps radio networks and stations. Users can filter by network, search with autocomplete, and click markers to zoom in and see details.</p>
      <p><strong>Technologies:</strong> Leaflet.js, JavaScript, HTML, CSS</p>
      <p><strong>My role:</strong> Developer on a 4 person team. I wrote the Sprint 4 retrospectives and usability testing documents.</p>
      <img src="https://github.com/AlexandrBalan/p48-radio-dashboard/blob/main/map1.png?raw=true" alt="Map of the United States with colored markers for radio stations and filter options on the side">
      <p><a href="https://github.com/AlexandrBalan/p48-radio-dashboard">GitHub Repo</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="project">
      <h2>Oceandive</h2>
      <p>A Game Boy Advance microgame where you swim in the ocean, dodge sharks, and collect fish.</p>
      <p><strong>Technologies:</strong> C++, GBA development, dev container, Git</p>
      <p><strong>My role:</strong> Developer on a 2 person team. We built the game together.</p>
      <img src="" alt="Oceandive game screen showing a scuba diver swimming toward a shark and fish">
      <p><a href="https://github.com/Ali200674/microjamC24">GitHub Repo</a></p>
    </section>
